{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal fails to adequately demonstrate that the development would not result in an increase in&nbsp; parking pressure along Southwold Drive and the wider area. As such the proposal is contrary to the following:Policy T6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMT 2&nbsp; of the&nbsp;Draft Local Plan",
    "The proposed development&nbsp;results in a loss of a large&nbsp;family-sized unit which is a priority house type within the Borough.&nbsp;As such, the proposal is considered unacceptable and contrary to the following:Policy BC4 of the Borough Wide DPD (March 2011); andPolicies SP 3 and DMH 5 of the&nbsp;Draft Local Plan 2037 Regulation 19 Main Modifications Version (Febraury 2024).",
    "The proposal proposes 3 double bedrooms which all fail to meet the minimum internal space standards, therefore would facilitate an inadequate quality of accommodation.&nbsp;&nbsp;As such, the proposal is considered unacceptable and contrary to the following:Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy BP6 of the Borough Wide DPD (March 2011)DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended)Housing Design Standards London Planning Guidance (June 2023)",
    "The proposed HMO has the potential to increase activity level and coming and goings to and from the site leading to additional levels of noise and disturbance at the property. This is considered to have a negative impact on neighbouring amenity in this street of family housing and in turn the health and wellbeing of neighbouring residents. As such the proposal is contrary to the following:Policies DMD 1, SP 7 and DMSI 3 of the Draft Local Plan; andPolicies BP8 and BP11 of the Borough Wide DPD (March 2011)."
  ],
